WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.934
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.934
As you guys know,
we're always striving

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:05.801
to get better here
at "The Tonight Show."

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:09.300
♪ Harder, better,
faster, stronger ♪

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.801
[ Laughter and cheers ]

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:13.434
So, before every show,
we put out a suggestion box

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.234
for the audience,
just to get some feedback

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:17.000
about what you guys think
of the show,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.000
things you'd like to see us do,
that kind of stuff.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.834
So, tonight, let's look inside
the Audience Suggestion Box.

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:22.834
Here we go.

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:23.834
-♪ Look into the box ♪

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:26.000
♪ The suggestion box ♪

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.334
[ Applause ]

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:28.834
-I appreciate these
suggestions, everybody.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.968
This first one
is from @Sherry --

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.801
It's not from "at," sorry.

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.968
This is from Sherry McFall.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:37.801
"Hey, Jimmy,
I love 'Yellowstone,'

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:40.133
and I'd love to hear
the theme song done with kazoos.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:41.300
Can you make that happen?"

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.667
Yeah, of course.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.634
Here's the theme from
"Yellowstone" done with kazoos.

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:46.968
Check it out.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:49.634
[ Kazoos playing ]

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:58.868
♪♪

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.267
There you go. That's not bad.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:01.934
They should use that.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:04.100
Yeah.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.234
Let's try another one here.
This one's from Dennis Harry.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:10.234
"Hey, Jimmy. I noticed there are
some buttons on your chair.

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:12.067
I was wondering
what those were for."

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:14.067
Oh, yeah. This is my --

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:15.400
This is my self-driving chair.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.400
-Oh!

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.567
-It's -- it's a brand-new thing.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:19.067
Just came out at CES.

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:21.067
And it's -- I'm one of
the firsts to have it.

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:22.234
-Wow.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:23.734
-It gets me around the studio
super fast.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:25.901
The chair just knows
where to go.

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.400
It's pretty -- you guys want
to see how it works?

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.734
[ Audience cheers ]

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.234
Here we go. Here.

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:33.400
You pull up the lever here,
like that.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.868
And then, here we go.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.200
Whoa!

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.033
This seat takes off.
Be right back.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:40.534
[ Wheels rattling ]
Whoo-hoo!

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:41.868
Watch out, watch out,
watch out, watch out!

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.033
Whoa!

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.667
Coming through!

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.167
Oww!

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.334
Aah!

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.767
Watch out! Whoa!

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:51.767
No, no, no.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.434
No, no, no, no!

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:55.100
[ Screaming ] Oh, God!

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.767
Oww!

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:57.934
Whoa-oh-oh-oh!

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.868
Aah!

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:02.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:07.267
-Wow!

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.601
Are you alright?

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.267
-What's that?
-Are you alright?

00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:11.934
-Perfectly great.

00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:14.100
-Did you say CES or CVS?

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.634
-We have another
suggestion here.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:18.934
This one's --

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.834
The chair gets me around
the studio.

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:23.033
-It doesn't look like
it's efficient, though.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.534
-Yeah.
Oh, it's fantastic.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:25.934
-Are you okay?
You seemed like you fell down

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:27.067
a few flights of stairs.
-What? No, no.

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:29.234
No! Was the --
Were the cameras on me?

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:30.901
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:34.234
-This is from Tracy Tompkins.

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:35.834
"Jimmy, I love virtual reality.

00:02:35.834 --> 00:02:38.501
You should have a VR interview
with someone on the show."

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:39.634
[ Audience murmurs ]

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:40.667
That's a great idea.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:41.667
We can actually try one
right now.

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:42.701
Tariq, are you down?

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:43.834
-Sure.
-Alright.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.334
Let me just put on
my headset here.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:47.501
Let's do this, man.
Here we go.

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:52.868
[ Chuckles ]
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:54.367
How's it going, Tariq?

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:57.133
-Oh, uh, pretty good.
Pretty good.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:59.234
-Any plans for the weekend?

00:02:59.234 --> 00:03:01.634
-Well, yeah, you know, I...

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:04.434
You know, I'mma go see "Avatar"

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:07.100
and also I have to do
some laundry.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.133
-Okay. I'm logging off.

00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:12.167
-Copy that.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:14.667
-Wow. That felt so real.

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.167
It felt like I was really
talking to you.

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:17.334
-I know. Yeah. Same here.

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:19.000
-It was wild.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.501
Amazing.
Amazing technology.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.667
Let's try another one.
It's from Erica Dale.

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:25.133
"Hey, Jimmy, I saw
the Property Brothers

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:26.434
were on the show last night.

00:03:26.434 --> 00:03:28.200
Can you have
the Property Brothers sing

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.033
the Righteous Brothers?"
-Oh!

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.734
-Well, yeah, I love
the Righteous Brothers.

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:34.033
So, ladies and gentlemen,
here are the Property Brothers

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:35.868
singing "You've Lost
That Lovin' Feelin'"

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:37.234
by the Righteous Brothers.

00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:38.234
Enjoy.

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:39.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:43.868
-♪ You never close your eyes
anymore ♪

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:47.534
♪ When I kiss your lips ♪

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:52.968
-♪ And there's no tenderness ♪

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:57.634
♪ Like before
in your fingertips ♪

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:04.200
-♪ You're trying hard
not to show it ♪

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.367
-♪ Baby ♪

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:09.033
-♪ But, baby ♪

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:12.367
♪ Baby, I know it ♪

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:17.868
-♪ You've lost
that lovin' feelin' ♪

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:23.033
♪ Whoa, that lovin' feelin' ♪

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:26.367
♪ You've lost
that lovin' feelin' ♪

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:30.534
♪ Now it's gone, gone, gone ♪

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.701
♪ Whoa-oh, whoa-oh ♪

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:34.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:36.567
-Wow.

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:38.901
-Wow!
-Come on.

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:40.234
-They were fantastic.

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:41.267
Property Brothers.
-They were delightful.

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:42.601
-I think they missed
their calling.

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:43.601
That's what they
should be doing.

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.067
I love that.
-Very well done.

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:48.067
-Here's another suggestion.
This one's from Gwen Noth.

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:50.901
"Hey, Jimmy, you never showed us
the virtual reality footage

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.400
from the interview you just did
with Tariq just now."

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.567
"Can we see it?"
Oh, yeah.

00:04:55.567 --> 00:04:56.968
Well, we couldn't
show it to you earlier,

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:59.133
because our camera systems don't
have the computing capacity

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:02.033
to render the graphics
at such a high frame rate.

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:03.868
But now it's fully rendered.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.534
Do you want to see it?
This is the actual...

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:06.868
[ Audience cheers ]

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:08.234
This is the actual VR footage

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:09.968
from me and Tariq's
interview earlier.

00:05:09.968 --> 00:05:11.634
-[Robotic voice] Tariq, hello.

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:13.701
How are you?
-Okay, Jimmy.

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:16.534
-What do your weekend plans?
Okay.

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:18.534
-I'm going to see "Avatar."

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:20.868
Laundry, laundry, laundry.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:22.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:24.467
-Can't get over how real --
it felt so real --

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:25.634
how real it looked.
-It felt like meta, metaverse.

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:26.968
-Amazing. Amazing.
-Yeah.

00:05:26.968 --> 00:05:28.801
-We're down to our last
suggestion here.

00:05:28.801 --> 00:05:30.133
It's from Nancy Bennion.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.300
It says, "Hey, Jimmy,
help settle a bet.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.133
I think the Wednesday Addams
dance is awesome.

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:36.300
But my friend likes

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.868
